Inlined some Triton-specific abstractions
* tensor is now just a container for dtype/shape with no extra methods;
* constexpr is not used;
* all APIs assume that the arguments are tensors and do no ->tensor conversion.
PiperOrigin-RevId: 603894852

Add function names to stack frames.
Also added optional filtering of internal stack frames and reversed callsite frame structure.
MLIR callsite expects first argument to be callee so we need to pass a first frame as a first argument.
The structure of call stack at MLIR now should look like this:
CallSiteLocation {
callee: {
NameLocation: { // New added structure
name: "function_name"
child_loc[FileLineColLoc]: {
filename: "filename"
line: 1
column: 0
}
}
}
caller [CallSiteLocation] {
// recursive
}
}
PiperOrigin-RevId: 547461060

Extend plugin discovery to also include entry-points.
This effectively implements a mix of option 2 and option 3 from https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/guides/creating-and-discovering-plugins/ as a pragmatic way to cover all packaging cases. The namespace/path based iteration works for situations where code has not been packaged and is present on the PYTHONPATH, whereas the advertised entry-points work around setuptools/pkgutil issues that make it impossible to reliably iterate over installed modules in certain scenarios (noted for editable installs which use a custom finder that does not implement iter_modules()).
A plugin entry-point can be advertised in setup.py (or equivalent pyproject.toml) with something like:
```
entry_points={
"jax_plugins": [
"openxla-cpu = jax_plugins.openxla_cpu",
],
}
```

fix comparison table in random docs
1. rbg is not identical across cpu/gpu/tpu;
2. the unsafe_rbg column copied the jax.lax.rng_uniform column from the original table, but that wasnt right, as it should be identical to the rbg column;
3. for the last row mentioning identical across shardings, we should mention that's assuming the xla flag
Also removed some rows which are only interesting in comparing to `jax.lax.rng_uniform` (which is not safe with `scan` or `remat`).
